		"authority": "Employment Act 1968 Part 4. s.38(4) — work beyond normal hours is paid at not less than one and a half times the hourly basic rate of pay (in this form since 1 March 1996, Act 36 of 1995). s.38(5) 72 overtime hours a month; s.38(8) 12 hours in any one day. s.38(1)(a) a break after more than 6 consecutive hours; s.38(1)(c) at least 45 minutes in the aggregate where work requiring continual attendance runs 8 consecutive hours. s.36 one rest day a week, and where a monthly roster is drawn up not more than 12 days between two rest days. s.37(3) rest-day pay at the employer's request. s.88 a public holiday falling on a rest day is observed on the next working day. s.35 and the First Schedule: Part 4 applies to a workman earning a basic monthly salary of not more than SGD 4,500 and to a non-workman (other than a manager or executive) earning not more than SGD 2,600."
	},
